```cpp
#include <algorithm>
#include <iostream>
#include <ranges>
#include <vector>

int main() {
    std::vector<int> nums{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6};
    std::ranges::sort(nums);                                   // whole-range algorithm.

    auto even_squares = nums
        | std::views::filter([](int n) { return n % 2 == 0; })
        | std::views::transform([](int n) { return n * n; });  // nothing computed yet.

    for (int x : even_squares) std::cout << x << ' ';           // 4 16 36 (computed now).

    std::vector<int> saved(even_squares.begin(), even_squares.end());  // materialise to keep.
    // nums.push_back(8);   while iterating even_squares: iterators may be invalidated.
}
```

| Idea | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `std::ranges::sort(v)`. | algorithm on a whole range. |
| `views::filter`, `views::transform`. | lazy steps in a pipeline. |
| view lifetime. | valid only while the source is alive and unchanged. |
| materialise. | copy into a container to keep results. |

